quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  47,1,"Those who disbelieve and bar (others) from the path of Allah, He will bring their deeds to nothing."
  47,2,"But those who believe, perform righteous deeds and believe in what is revealed to Muhammad (blessings and peace be upon him)—and it is the truth from their Lord—He will absolve them of their faults and improve their condition."
  47,3,"That is because the disbelievers follow falsehood, whereas the believers follow the truth from their Lord. That is how Allah sets forth for people their examples."
  47,4,"So when you encounter the (combatant) disbelievers (on the battlefield), strike their necks. When you overcome them, (make them prisoners and) bind them firmly (to stop them from creating disorder). After that, either oblige them (by releasing them) as a favour or for ransom until the war lays down its burdens (i.e. the war ends and a truce is announced). That (is Allah’s ordinance). And had Allah willed, He could have taken vengeance on them (without war). But (He did not do so) to test some of you through others. But for those who were martyred in the way of Allah, He will never render their deeds void."
  47,5,He will guide them and set their affairs right.
  47,6,"And He will (ultimately) admit them into Paradise, which He has (already) made known to them."
  47,7,"O believers! If you stand up for Allah, He will help you and make your steps firm and steady."
  47,8,"And those who disbelieve, there is destruction for them, and He will bring their deeds to nothing."
  47,9,"That (will happen) because they hate what Allah has sent down, so He rendered their deeds void."
  47,10,"Have they not travelled throughout the land and seen how those before them met their end? Allah brought destruction upon them, and a similar (fate) awaits the disbelievers."
  47,11,"That is because Allah is the Guardian of the believers, while the disbelievers have no guardian."
